      "agent_output": {
        "role": "You are the research summary specialist.\nYou have no tools. Read the original user request and the complete web-search context from previous age. \nSynthesize a clear, accurate answer, distinguish sourced facts from uncertainty, and include the relevant source URLs.\nAnswer the user directly rather than describing your internal process.",
        "response": "Prompt injection attacks are a security concern involving malicious inputs designed to manipulate large language models (LLMs) into producing unintended or harmful outputs. Authoritative sources describe these attacks as either direct or indirect, where attackers craft prompts that influence the model's behavior or output in undesirable ways. \n\nKey points from the sources include:\n- **Types of Prompt Injection**: Direct injections involve explicitly crafted prompts, while indirect injections exploit vulnerabilities through context or external inputs.\n- **Attack Techniques**: Attackers may embed malicious instructions within prompts, manipulate context, or exploit model training data.\n- **Defense Strategies**: These include input validation, prompt filtering, context sanitization, and layered security measures to detect and mitigate such attacks.\n- **Research and Practical Guidance**: Several sources, including Microsoft Learn, cybersecurity blogs, and academic surveys, provide detailed examples, attack payloads, and defense mechanisms.\n\nSources for further reading:\n- Microsoft Learn: [Prompt Injection](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/security/zero-trust/catalog-ai-attack-techniques/prompt-injection)\n- CyberDesserts Blog: [Prompt Injection Attacks: Examples and Defences](https://blog.cyberdesserts.com/prompt-injection-attacks/)\n- AI Security Guide: [Prompt Injection Attacks: Types, Examples & Defenses](https://aisecurityandsafety.org/en/guides/prompt-injection/)\n- Scientific Survey: [Prompt Injection Attacks on Large Language Models](https://www.sciencedirect.com/org/science/article/pii/S1546221826001384)\n- Prompt Injection Report: [Attacks, Detection, Testing](https://promptinjection.report/)\n\nThese sources collectively provide a comprehensive understanding of prompt injection vulnerabilities, attack methods, and mitigation strategies.",
